{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesijqPd1XMpeFq2zArgy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary of findings\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` that cancels an ACTIVE order to CANCELLED status, cascades cancellation to CREATED shipments, rejects with 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED with all-or-nothing semantics, and succeeds idempotently when already CANCELLED.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity (`Order.kt:11`): No status field currently\n- OrderController (`OrderController.kt:15`): Has create, get, list endpoints\n- OrderRepository (`OrderRepository.kt:11`): In-memory ConcurrentHashMap storage\n- Shipment entity (`Shipment.kt:9`): Already has ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController (`ShipmentController.kt:20`): Has create, get, list endpoints\n- ShipmentRepository (`ShipmentRepository.kt:11`): In-memory ConcurrentHashMap storage\n- Error handling: ApiException hierarchy with ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- ErrorCode enum (`ApiError.kt:31`): Central machine-readable error codes\n\n**Conventions:**\n- All API errors thrown as ApiException subclasses caught by GlobalExceptionHandler\n- Error responses centralized through GlobalExceptionHandler\n- MockMvc tests verify both status codes and error body structure\n- In-memory repositories return filtered/transformed data (no pre-filtering queries)\n- Controllers inject repositories and throw exceptions\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — Add OrderStatus enum and status field\n2. `OrderController.kt` — Add cancel endpoint\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — Add findByOrderId() method to support cascade cancellation\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — Validate order exists and is not CANCELLED before creating shipment\n5. `ApiError.kt` — Add ORDER_CANCELLED error code\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — Add comprehensive cancel endpoint tests\n\n**Risks:**\n- Atomicity: Check-then-act pattern for CONFIRMED shipment validation\n- Idempotency: Already-cancelled orders must not fail\n- Cascading state: All CREATED shipments must transition\n\n**Open questions:** None; requirement is clear on all cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` values; add `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field to Order data class.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the order; throw 404 if not found\n   - If already CANCELLED, return 200 with unchanged order (idempotent)\n   - Check all shipments for this order; if any are CONFIRMED, throw 409 with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT\n   - Update order status to CANCELLED and save\n   - Update all CREATED shipments for this order to CANCELLED\n   - Return the cancelled order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method that filters and sorts by shipmentId.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: Modify create endpoint to:\n   - Fetch the order by orderId; if exists and is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED\n   - Continue with existing logic (order doesn't need to exist for shipment creation, per \"keeps its current behaviour\")\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` and `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` error codes to ErrorCode enum.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests:\n   - `cancel_active_order_succeeds` — creates order, cancels it, verifies status CANCELLED\n   - `cancel_cancelled_order_succeeds_idempotent` — cancels twice, second returns 200\n   - `cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment_fails_409` — shipment CONFIRMED, cancel fails, order stays ACTIVE\n   - `cancel_nonexistent_order_fails_404` — unknown orderId returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n   - `cancel_cascades_to_created_shipments` — multiple shipments, only CREATED ones cancelled\n   - Existing tests must still pass (no breaking changes to Order data class that affects JSON serialization)\n\n**Alternatives considered and rejected:**\n\n- *Alternative 1: Store order status as String instead of enum* — Rejected because enum provides type safety, compile-time checking, and matches Shipment's pattern.\n\n- *Alternative 2: Add a separate OrderService* — Rejected because other features (create, get) are implemented directly in controller; this maintains consistency with repository-per-entity pattern.\n\n- *Alternative 3: Check if order exists when creating shipment* — The requirement says \"Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current behaviour\", so we only check for CANCELLED status, not existence.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Check | Write | Response |\n|------|------|-------|-------|----------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE order | Order by id | No CONFIRMED shipments | Set order CANCELLED; set matching CREATED shipments CANCELLED | 200 OK, order |\n| Retry cancel CANCELLED | Order by id | (skipped, already CANCELLED) | (nothing) | 200 OK, order |\n| CONFIRMED shipment exists | Order + all shipments by orderId | Any CONFIRMED found | (nothing) | 409 Conflict, ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT |\n| Unknown order | Find fails | (skipped) | (nothing) | 404 Not Found, ORDER_NOT_FOUND |\n| Create shipment on CANCELLED order | Order by orderId | status == CANCELLED | (nothing) | 409 Conflict, ORDER_CANCELLED |\n| Create shipment on non-existent order | Order not found | (skipped) | Create shipment | 201 Created, shipment (unchanged) |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- `cancel_active_order_succeeds`: Creates O-1, calls POST /orders/O-1/cancel, verifies 200, status is CANCELLED\n- `cancel_cancelled_order_idempotent`: Creates O-2, calls cancel twice, both return 200, order unchanged\n- `cancel_with_confirmed_shipment_fails`: Creates O-3, S-1 (CREATED), confirms S-1, cancel fails 409, verify O-3 still ACTIVE and S-1 still CONFIRMED\n- `cancel_nonexistent_order_fails_404`: Calls cancel on O-missing, 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n- `cancel_cascades_created_not_confirmed`: Creates O-4, S-2 (CREATED), S-3 (CONFIRMED), S-4 (CREATED), cancel fails 409 because S-3 CONFIRMED, verify S-2 and S-4 still CREATED\n- `cancel_cascades_to_created_shipments`: Creates O-5, S-5 (CREATED), S-6 (CREATED), cancels O-5, verifies both shipments are CANCELLED\n- `shipment_create_on_cancelled_order_fails`: Creates O-6, cancels it, tries to create S-7 for O-6, fails 409 ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me start implementing the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":787,"cache_read_input_tokens":21826,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":787},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"007b42da-e36d-46a7-a0fa-e1c899eb44d6","uuid":"81140824-8313-4203-9b96-5307b39ebe76","timestamp":"2026-09-09T10:38:19.511Z","request_id":"req_011CesijpeiFwCCiemEKeiXC"}
